 "notes": "Withdrawn list (godigit.com/life/withdrawn-products; HTML S.No|Name|UIN|documents, no dates) has 23 rows but only 10 distinct UINs (Icon variants and a duplicated Group Micro Term row collapsed). Active list built from live product pages and brochures: Glow Plus 165N007V03 (brochure as on 2 Jul 2026), Glow Lite 165N006V01, ICON 165N011V04 (page disclaimer still shows V03), Digit Life Pension Plan 165N032V01 (launched 15 Jul 2026; UIN from KID/CIS PDFs). Quarterly product-disclosure PDFs and /life/other-product-documents returned client_error, so active group versions are unconfirmed: the site still has pages for Group Term Life, Group Long Term Plan and Group Micro Term, but only V01 UINs appear (as withdrawn). Glow Lite is placed in segment Micro (page calls it a micro term plan; SA cap Rs 2 lakh). Digit Life Healthy Glow Policy (withdrawn) has a general-insurer style UIN (GODHLIP25032V012425); its category is a best guess. No separate riders with UINs found: ADB and ATPD are optional benefits inside Glow Plus/Lite. Conflict: Glow Plus web page says term 5-40 yrs and min SA Rs 10 lakh, brochure says term up to 67 yrs and min SA Rs 2.25 lakh (brochure used). Pension Plan marketing pages (guaranteed-pension-plans, annuity) are generic and show no UIN. Business Standard (2023-06-26) reports the maiden product was a group term plan."
